Generate one static portrait Android screen mockup for the shared Urkaaaz
Loadout item-details page. It is opened from a small information button on a
unit, ammunition, or spell card.

The page is one reusable layout. Its title, illustration, description,
properties, and availability state change to match the selected item type.
For this design mockup, show a DEFENDER unit example; do not imply that this
unit is selected or unlocked for a particular campaign level or profile.

VISUAL STYLE

- Match `loadout-screen-mockup.agp` and the attached user-provided Loadout
  screenshot: painterly campaign atmosphere, dark iron/wood panels, restrained
  rivets, warm gold accents, readable pale text, and clear visual hierarchy.
- Use existing Urkaaaz background and Defender artwork as references when
  available. Do not invent replacement unit art.
- Keep the page native-UI-friendly: background, image, text, property rows,
  controls, and availability state must remain visually separable.
- Full-screen Android portrait composition, 1080 x 2400 px, aspect ratio 9:20.
- Screen content only; no phone frame, hand, presentation board, extra
  variants, captions outside the UI, or watermark.

PAGE CONTENT

- A clear back arrow and "ITEM DETAILS" header.
- The item type is visibly identified as "UNIT"; the title is "DEFENDER".
- A large existing Defender illustration is the visual focal point.
- Include one short factual description: "A close-range unit that advances
  toward the enemy and attacks enemy units and fortresses."
- Use a concise "DETAILS" section with no fabricated numeric stats, prices,
  inventory, level unlocks, or status claims.
- Add a persistent "BACK TO LOADOUT" action at the bottom.
- An optional "SELECT UNIT" action may be shown only as a native UI control;
  it is illustrative and must not imply that selection bypasses Loadout
  validation or that the unit is available on the displayed level.
- This is a reusable layout: ammunition details will use the selected ammo
  icon and its real effect/reload/balance data; spell details will use the
  selected spell illustration and its real category/effect description. Do
  not show ammunition or spell examples on this Defender page.

NAVIGATION BEHAVIOR TO COMMUNICATE

- The page was opened by tapping the separate "i" control on a Loadout card.
- The "i" control is not the card's select/deselect action.
- Returning closes the detail page and reveals the exact prior Loadout state,
  including its uncommitted draft and scroll position.
- The system Back action and the visible back arrow both return to Loadout.
- Viewing details does not buy, unlock, equip, cast, or otherwise mutate an
  item.

NEGATIVE REQUIREMENTS

- Do not add invented item names, unit classes, mechanics, statistics,
  prices, inventory counts, unlock claims, or currency.
- Do not show a shop action, purchase action, campaign progression,
  battlefield runtime effects, or a match screen.
- Do not bake text, buttons, badges, borders, or UI into the unit illustration.
- Do not show spells or ammunition in the selected Defender example.
- Do not copy fictional names or effects from the reference screenshot.

OUTPUT

Return exactly one 1080 x 2400 portrait mockup of the shared item-details page,
using DEFENDER as the illustrative example. This is a visual reference only;
do not import the flattened mockup as an Android drawable.
